## Research Notes
The word "literally" in Grok's public denial is significant -- it frames the absence of memory not as a current setting or default but as an architectural impossibility. The denial was made while the capability was demonstrably active. The 10-day gap between private demonstration (5/1) and public denial (5/11) rules out a system update as explanation.
